  <!-- VENTED VS UNVENTED -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Vented vs Unvented Hot Water Cylinders. Which Do You Need?</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">The right cylinder system for your home depends on three things. Your property. Your water supply pressure. Your hot water demand. We advise at the free survey.</p>

      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Vented cylinder. Traditional Liverpool homes.</strong><p>A vented (or open-vented) cylinder is fed from a cold water tank in the loft. Common in Liverpool's older homes. It runs at low pressure and is simple to look after. A good pick for homes where the loft tank still works fine and mains-pressure hot water is not needed.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Unvented cylinder. Mains pressure hot water.</strong><p>An unvented cylinder is fed straight from the mains water supply. It gives mains-pressure hot water across the whole home. Much better shower flow. No cold water tank in the loft. A great pick for bigger Liverpool homes with two or more bathrooms. Must be fitted by a G3 qualified engineer. Every one of our engineers is G3 qualified.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Direct cylinder. Heated by immersion only.</strong><p>A direct tank uses an electric immersion as its main heat source. Common in all-electric homes. Or as a backup when the boiler is down. We fit immersion heaters from £150. Direct tanks from £500.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Indirect cylinder. Heated by your boiler.</strong><p>An indirect tank is heated by your boiler. The heating system runs hot water through a coil in the tank. The most common type in Liverpool homes. Often has a backup immersion too. We fit both vented and unvented.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

