      <h2>Hot Water Cylinder Installation Liverpool. Your Questions Answered</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Straight answers to what Liverpool homeowners ask most before booking.</p>
      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does a hot water cylinder cost in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A vented indirect cylinder fitted starts at £600. Unvented starts at £900. Immersion swap from £150. Prices depend on size, type and access. We give a free fixed-price quote after a site visit.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">TYPES</span>&nbsp; What is the difference between vented and unvented?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A vented cylinder is fed from a cold water tank in the loft and runs at low pressure. Common in Liverpool's older homes. An unvented cylinder is fed from the mains and gives hot water at mains pressure. Better shower flow. No loft tank. Unvented must be fitted by a G3 qualified engineer.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COMBI</span>&nbsp; Should I get a cylinder or a combi boiler?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A combi boiler heats water on demand. No cylinder needed. A good fit for smaller Liverpool homes with one bathroom. Bigger homes with two or more bathrooms or high hot water demand do better with a system boiler and an unvented cylinder. You get mains-pressure hot water at every tap with no run-out. We advise at the free survey.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">SIZE</span>&nbsp; What size hot water cylinder do I need?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>It depends on your home. 130 litres for a small flat. 200 litres for a 2-bed home. 250 litres for a 3-bed home with one or two bathrooms. 300 litres or more for big family homes. We work out the right size at the free survey.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">BRANDS</span>&nbsp; What hot water cylinder brands do you fit?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We fit cylinders from Megaflo, Worcester Bosch, OSO, Telford, RM Cylinders, Joule and Gledhill. Standard, premium and speciality types all in the range. Heat pump and solar coil cylinders too. Tell us your needs and we will spec the right one.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">SERVICE</span>&nbsp; Do unvented cylinders need an annual service?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Unvented cylinders need a service every year. The law says so. The maker's warranty says so. Our annual G3 service starts at £120. Or pair it with a boiler service for £175. We send a service reminder each year.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">TIME</span>&nbsp; How long does cylinder installation take?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A vented swap takes 4 to 6 hours. An unvented fit takes 6 to 8 hours. A back-of-bath fit can take a full day if the access is tight. We give a clear time at the free survey. Most jobs done in one visit.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">G3</span>&nbsp; Are you qualified to install unvented cylinders?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Unvented fits need the G3 cert under Part G of the Building Regs. All our team who fit unvented hold this cert. Every job is notified. You get a certificate to keep. Never let a plumber without G3 fit an unvented tank.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are you Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We are on the Gas Safe register. You can check us at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. All cylinder fits are done by Gas Safe registered engineers. All gas work is carried out by Gas Safe registered engineers.</p></div></details>
